From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:48:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Keep the compute queue state off the
 boot stack

Engine and Graphs are built by value in Firmware::start_backend, and
the whole Firmware is moved in Firmware::orphan_firmware. The compute
queue fields added for g16_compute_queues and g16_cq_split_us
(per-queue targets, ordinals, heads, registration, publication counts
and stage stamps) and the code that makes the objects of compute
queues 1.. made start_backend's frame 480 bytes larger than in the
previous release kernel. A kernel stack overflow at boot was already
seen once from such growth.

Move these Engine fields into one heap object, ComputeQueues, built in
its own non-inlined function, so that Engine carries only a pointer.
Make the objects of compute queues 1.. in two non-inlined functions,
called at the same points as before, so the allocation order and every
object's address stay as they were. The fields keep their meaning;
only their path changes from engine.cq_X to engine.cq.X. No behaviour
change.

Assisted-by: LLM
